 # Ray-marched Shadows
 
-Also called: Hard Shadow Ray Marching, Hard Shadows, Hard Shadows via Sphere Tracing, SDF Shadow Ray Marching, SDF Shadows
+Also called: Hard Shadow Casting, Hard Shadow Ray Marching, Hard Shadows, Hard Shadows via Sphere Tracing, SDF Shadow Ray Marching, SDF Shadows
 
 ## Overview
-Ray-marched shadows determine if a surface point is occluded from a light source by performing sphere tracing along a ray directed from the surface point toward the light [S1, S2, S3, S8, S10, unofficial]. Unlike [Distance Color Blending](791-distance-color-blending.md) which blends colors based on depth, this method returns a binary occlusion factor (0 for shadow, 1 for light) by checking if the Signed Distance Field (SDF) drops below a threshold before the ray reaches the light [S7, S10, unofficial]. It differs from [Shadow Casting Algorithm](1657-shadow-casting-algorithm.md) by leveraging the global geometric information inherent in the SDF, requiring no separate shadow map pass or rasterization overhead [S9, S12, unofficial].
